<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ai.ted.logs</string>

  <!-- T35's other half: old logs expiring predictably.

       The content half was closed by Hermes patch 14, which withholds the
       message text in the gateway itself, and is verified: there is not one
       real user word in the live logs. What was never built is expiry. The
       tool to do it has existed since 18 Sep and ran only when somebody
       thought to type it, which is the same shape as every other thing this
       project has had to schedule.

       04:30, half an hour after ai.ted.backup. Deliberate order: a log is
       copied into the backup before anything prunes it, so the retention
       window never eats the only copy of a day nobody has looked at yet.

       30 days, which is the window the script's own usage line has suggested
       since it was written. It is a decision rather than a law: these logs
       now hold metadata, not health content, so the cost of keeping them is
       disk and the cost of losing them is a diagnosis. Change the number here
       if a real investigation ever needs longer.

       It rewrites nothing the gateway has open. A live log is reported and
       left, which is the script's own rule and the reason a rotated log is
       the only thing this can actually clean. That is fine: the rotations are
       where the bulk sits.

       Exit code 0 is a real signal here. The job exits non-zero only when a
       live log genuinely still holds user text, which would mean patch 14 has
       regressed, and that is worth waking up for.

       The interpreter is the Hermes venv's, not /usr/bin/python3: macOS
       refuses a launchd agent access to ~/Documents unless that binary has
       been granted it. See the same note in ai.ted.backup.plist. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/Documents/build-week-health accountability partner/scripts/ted-log-retention.py</string>
    <string>--scrub</string>
    <string>--days</string>
    <string>30</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>4</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>30</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-log-retention.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/vandana.agarwal/.hermes/logs/ted-log-retention.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
